   The effect estimates are facts reported in the cited publications. Each row names its source DOI.
   The column `evidence_quote` holds short verbatim excerpts (usually under 300 characters) so each
   number can be checked. Excerpts are included ONLY for sources published under CC BY (any version)
   or CC0. For every other source (CC BY-NC, CC BY-NC-ND, publisher free-access terms, publisher
   copyright) the excerpt is left blank and `evidence_quote_status` says why; the number, DOI and
   location are still given. The excerpts that are included remain the work of the original authors
   under the source article's CC BY or CC0 licence (column `license` in data/sources.csv); they are
   attributed by the DOI in the same row.

2. Code (scripts/, tests/): MIT License.

